<section id="1001I_S000I" variety="S000I">
<name>Door Lock</name>
<ttl id="1001I_S000I_744CL_T004H" variety="T004H">
<name>Smart Entry &amp; Start System (Smart Entry)</name>
<para id="RM000002QWZ003X" category="J" type-id="802XH" name-id="622PO-00" from="200612">
<dtccode/>
<dtcname>Smart Lock and Unlock Do Not Operate from Any Door (Wireless Function Also Does Not Operate)</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM000002QWZ003X_02" type-id="33" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___000029M00000">
<name>Function Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<ptxt>If the door lock function by smart operation and wireless operation does not operate, a malfunction in the area common to the smart function and wireless function (door control receiver -&gt; certification ECU signal circuit, electronic key, interference from radio waves) is suspected.</ptxt>
<atten3>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>The Smart Entry &amp; Start System (smart entry) has functions that use multiplex communication. First, follow "How to Proceed with Troubleshooting" and confirm that there is no malfunction in the communication system before proceeding with troubleshooting.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>When using TaSCAN with the IG OFF, repeatedly turn any door courtesy light switch ON &lt;-&gt; OFF until communication between TaSCAN and the vehicle starts. (ON←→OFF interval within 1.5 seconds)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>When the electrical key transmitter (electronic key) or smart key computer assembly (certification ECU) is replaced, refer to the immobiliser registration procedure in the reference section.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Check that there are no other electrical key transmitters in the vehicle interior.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten3>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000002QWZ003X_03" type-id="32" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___000029N00000">
<name>Wiring Diagram</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="B167039J01" width="7.106578999in" height="4.7836529in"/>
</figure>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000002QWZ003X_04" type-id="51" category="05">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000002QWZ003X_01" type-id="01" category="01">
<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="RM000002QWZ003X_01_0002" proc-id="RM0550J___000029G00000">
<testtitle>Inspect Power Door Lock System</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<test1>
<ptxt>Check that the door locks operate lock - unlock when the door control switch of the power window regulator master switch assembly is operated.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Result</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="2" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.50in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.63in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Result</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Proceed to</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Operates normally</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>A</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Does not operate normally</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>B</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000002QWZ003X_01_0003" fin="false">A</down>
<right ref="RM000002QWZ003X_01_0010" fin="true">B</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
