<testgrp id="RM000002QWZ003X_01_0011" proc-id="RM0550J___000029L00000">
<testtitle>Inspect Transmitter Battery (Voltage Inspection)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Remove the transmitter battery from the electrical key transmitter (electronic key).</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance of the transmitter battery.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Voltage</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.26in"/>
<colspec colname="COLSPEC0" colwidth="0.92in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="0.95in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Tester Connection</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Transmitter battery positive - Transmitter battery negative</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>2.1 to 3.2 V</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000002QWZ003X_01_0014" fin="true">OK</down>
<right ref="RM000002QWZ003X_01_0015" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000002QWZ003X_01_0004" proc-id="RM0550J___000029I00000">
<testtitle>Radio Wave Environment Check</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<test1>
<ptxt>Perform wireless operation with the electrical key transmitter held close to the door control receiver, and check the operation.</ptxt>
<atten4>
<ptxt>Holding the electrical key transmitter close to the door control receiver makes it less susceptible to radio interference, so it can be determined whether radio interference is the cause.</ptxt>
</atten4>
<spec>
<title>Result</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="2" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.44in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.69in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Result</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Proceed to</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Does not operate normally</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>A</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Operates normally</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>B</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
<atten4>
<ptxt>If the inspection result is "OK", radio interference or reduced output of the electronic key is suspected. If the system does not operate only at specific locations or times, radio interference is likely. Also, dealer-installed parts, etc. (mobile phone charger, power outlet [AC100V power supply], etc.) may cause radio interference, so if there are dealer-installed parts, remove them and check the operation.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000002QWZ003X_01_0006" fin="false">A</down>
<right ref="RM000002QWZ003X_01_0005" fin="true">B</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000002QWZ003X_01_0005">
<testtitle>Effect of interfering radio waves</testtitle>
</testgrp>
